  "moderate_issues_authored": {
    "shared_cut_and_state": {"category":"diversity","severity":"moderate","evidence":"All216 initial states are(2,2), all twelve F traces share the first seven complete events, R histories/checkpoints are identical and P full outputs are identical. The remaining family graph differences are real but mostly occur after this common core.","fix":"In a fresh generator/version vary actual initial state, retained binding values, interruption locations and caller contexts while maintaining matched controls. Count twelve programs, not216 independent examples or108 mechanisms.","nonblocking_reason":"The public pilot declares correlated views and a finite exact execution proxy; actual required relationships and full outputs are correct. No arbitrary-cut or broad-transfer coverage is approved."},
    "true_branch_child_success_only": {"category":"shortcut_resistance","severity":"moderate","evidence":"All288 newly committed branch choices are true, all456 new child entries pass initiation and all504 child returns pass success. Failures are confined to root I/S; selected suspended guards can be currently false, which is a different real resumption mechanism.","fix":"Add matched executed else choices, nonroot entry/exit failures and terminal checkpoints to a separate prospective batch; handmade test coverage is not corpus coverage.","nonblocking_reason":"The nine public pilot contexts require root guard contrasts and retained-selection behavior, both actually witnessed. Broader child-failure/else coverage is explicitly unestablished."},
    "status_and_output_redundancy": {"category":"shortcut_resistance","severity":"moderate","evidence":"120/216 completed and24 each paused/initiation_failed/success_failed/invalid. Fitted status majority/mode/history cues reach55.56%, and budget or mode/history/budget reaches66.67%; only75 full outputs occur among108 semantic tasks. These are corpus diagnostics, not learner results.","fix":"Use full typed target evaluation, report conditional tables and redundancy, and cross outcome statuses with varied valid modes/budgets/history lengths prospectively.","nonblocking_reason":"A status heuristic does not reproduce the full events, bindings, checkpoint and next-event object for complex rows. Public design already scopes this finite controlled pilot rather than a shortcut-free benchmark."},
    "exposed_dev_and_finite_programs": {"category":"generalization_value","severity":"moderate","evidence":"Four exposed-dev families (indices18,19,28,29) share primitive motifs and the same interruption core with eight train families. The legacy24 views collapse to8 graph signatures, while twelve new families are distinct in all three own normalizations with zero legacy collisions. This is structural separation, not empirical transfer or independent-model evidence.","fix":"Preserve family-level splits and public exposure labels; later preregister a held-out composition/state/cut study. Do not infer model improvement from these data.","nonblocking_reason":"All descendants of each family remain in one split and actual graph novelty is truthful at the published normalization. The narrow interpreter-training use remains supported."},
    "generic_difficulty_description": {"category":"difficulty_quality","severity":"moderate","evidence":"Exactly192 rows share one generic Level3 explanation and24 root-I rows have a specific Level2 explanation. P has one new effect plus a peek; X has zero legal future events. Their difficulty rests on supplied history/snapshot validation, not on all later family work.","fix":"In a future metadata version write context-specific descriptions distinguishing full continuation, validated short pause, root exit test and checkpoint mismatch, and measure work required to prove each result.","nonblocking_reason":"Level3 compound validation is permitted by R1 and is present, but explanations are weak for P/X and are scored3. No difficulty4..7 or long-horizon claim is approved."},
    "generic_skill_descriptors": {"category":"competency","severity":"moderate","evidence":"Every row has the same finite_synthetic_proxy/supplied_option_execution/versioned_checkpoint_validation descriptors. I is a root-entry component; F/A/S construct fresh snapshots rather than challenge a supplied checkpoint. These are treated as interface/cohort descriptors, not evidence that every row exercises all checkpoint mechanisms.","fix":"Add accurate context-specific competency descriptions alongside format/cohort descriptors without changing the student task or fabricating per-row property witnesses.","nonblocking_reason":"The actual instruction and public context define each narrower competency; generic private descriptors do not alter gold or leak an answer. This assessment explicitly limits their interpretation."}
